units.raw:
3.1 The obligations imposed on the Receiving Party under Clause 2 shall not apply to any portion of information which the Receiving Party can prove by contemporaneous written documentation:
3.1.1 was already in the lawful possession of the Receiving Party prior to disclosure by or on behalf of the Disclosing Party, without obligation of confidentiality;
3.1.2 is or becomes publicly available through no breach of this Agreement, fault, act, or omission of the Receiving Party or its Representatives;
3.1.3 is rightfully received by the Receiving Party on a non-confidential basis from an independent third party having the lawful right to make such disclosure without breaching any legal, contractual, or fiduciary obligation; or
3.1.4 has been independently developed by employees or agents of the Receiving Party without reference to, reliance upon, incorporation of, or access to any of the Disclosing Party's Confidential Information.

